/*
Our goal is to make our query more efficient. In order to do this we need to get the computer to do less things.
Two things we can eliminate for the computer are typecasting as well as subtraction. This attempt shows how I do that.
*/

SELECT DISTINCT num AS ConsecutiveNums
FROM (
    SELECT num, LEAD(num) OVER(ORDER BY id) as OneAhead, LEAD(num, 2) OVER(ORDER BY id) as TwoAhead
    FROM logs
)
WHERE OneAhead = num AND TwoAhead = num;




/*
This method provides a much more efficient run time as the computer does not have to typecast or do subtraction.
Over a large dataset, that could save lots of power and money.
In addition we have made our code type agnostic. When we used subtraction, it made it so our query would only pull things that are the same number 
three times consecutively. Now, any value that is repeated three times in a row will show up.
